<title>RUSSIA: Russian confectioner sells 45 pct for $5.5 mln.</title>
<headline>Russian confectioner sells 45 pct for $5.5 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's sixth biggest confectionery factory OAO Volzhanka has sold 45 percent of its shares in a public offering for $5.5 million, the factory's financial adviser Creditanstalt-Grant said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The factory, located in Ulyanovsk on the Volga river, sold about 5.71 million shares with a face value of 1,000 roubles to big Western investment funds, Creditanstalt-Grant said in a statement.</p>
<p>Further details will be given in a news conference on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
